    tmk:supportingText "A trade mark is likely to cause confusion if the ordinary person entertains a reasonable doubt about whether the goods and services come from the same source." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0102 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0008 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:qualifies ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0011 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual reproduces judicial principles requiring consideration of surrounding circumstances when assessing likelihood of deception or confusion. Reading this with principle (i), those circumstances inform assessment of the real tangible danger threshold, rather than alter that threshold."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the connection through likelihood of deception or confusion sufficiently supports qualifies for the danger threshold itself."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0102" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:modality "must" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:be7ebe89c273e99bd6bdd4f0a39584903353c1236cad36f992403c53c447dcc8" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/2%231> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 1594 ;
    tmk:spanStart 1451 ;
    tmk:supportingText "(iii) In considering whether there is a likelihood of deception or confusion all surrounding circumstances have to be taken into consideration." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0103 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0004 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:qualifies ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0011 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual expressly treats potentially mitigating surrounding circumstances as relevant to its stated criteria for confusion from a standalone geographical reference. This supports qualification of the confusion assessment, not a general rule that surrounding circumstances prevent confusion."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.6e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether this relationship should be restricted to confusion arising from standalone geographical references."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0103" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:67e2721f9a84ad01289f7b3ee6a65ec86e7be0a016c468e3eb7c3094b6166356" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/9/9/3~1> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 723 ;
    tmk:spanStart 609 ;
    tmk:supportingText "There are no other elements in the mark, or surrounding circumstances, which would mitigate the risk of confusion." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0104 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0003 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:qualifies ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0011 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual directs that surrounding circumstances should be considered in assessing likelihood of deception or confusion in the goods-and-services context. They therefore qualify that assessment rather than independently establish deception."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.3e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the relationship needs an express limitation to the assessment involving goods and services discussed here."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0104" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:modality "should" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:1388f5f15605b8ae58b2db5db22a66ceb75d846aa24d831d205a819647fc6892" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/4/4/3~2> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 1591 ;
    tmk:spanStart 1016 ;
    tmk:supportingText "In assessing the likelihood of deception or confusion in a case of goods and services, consideration should be given to consumer expectations. Factors which influence consumer expectations include whether the services are performed upon, in relation to, or by means of certain goods. Consideration should also be given to the marketplace realities and surrounding circumstances including: the circumstances in which the marks will be used, the circumstances in which the goods or services will be bought and sold, and the character of the consumers of the goods and services." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0105 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0010 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate skos:related ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0011 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The reproduced judicial principles include the character of probable acquirers among surrounding circumstances. This supports a connection with the ordinary-consumer concept, although identifying probable acquirers with that concept is an inference rather than an express equivalence."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7.8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the character of probable acquirers should be mapped to ordinary consumer or recorded as a separate factor."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0105" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:be7ebe89c273e99bd6bdd4f0a39584903353c1236cad36f992403c53c447dcc8" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/2%231> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 1804 ;
    tmk:spanStart 1595 ;
    tmk:supportingText "These include the circumstances in which the marks will be used, the circumstances in which the goods and services will be bought and sold and the character of the probable acquirers of the goods and services." ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

tmka:GR-0106 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0012 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:appliesTo ;
