    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "4.1.1 If an application for deferment has been made on the ground that a pending application has been cited against the application and that citation has the same filing date as the application for which the request for deferral has been made, that request will be denied." ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

tmka:GR-0317 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0157 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate skos:related ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0141 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual connects the date of registration with the application date in a Convention country where priority is claimed under subsection 29(b). No listed specific predicate precisely captures that conditional date-setting relationship between these two concepts."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether dependsOnExternalSource is intended to include a country as shorthand for the application made there."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0317" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:89731caeea8ffb9d5371c5a8a72850578ab0daf6b0ce412ab95a7a004e4b78e0" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/7%231~1> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 1253 ;
    tmk:spanStart 1093 ;
    tmk:supportingText "In the latter case the date of registration will be the date on which the application was made in the Convention country in respect of those goods and services." ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

tmka:GR-0318 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0153 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:requiresElement ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0103 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual identifies an adequate statement of grounds and particulars as one component of a complete notice of opposition, not as the whole notice. Other sentences in this passage inconsistently refer to an intention to defend as the other component."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.6e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The inconsistent references to intention to defend versus intention to oppose in this passage."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0318" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:681326c5b886f57abbad8ea0908be029fd73ae3ddb1753a4f5a70da40b049eca" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part60/4/17/4/17/2~2> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 1800 ;
    tmk:spanStart 1558 ;
    tmk:supportingText "When a complete Notice of Opposition is filed (that is, a notice of intention to oppose, together with an adequate statement of grounds and particulars), IP Australia will record it on the Trade Marks Office database and notify the IB as soon" ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0319 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0158 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate skos:related ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0153 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual connects filing the statement, as part of a complete notice of opposition, with the subsequent conditional obligation to file a notice of intention to defend. It does not describe the statement as a component of the defence notice."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The limitation of the quoted obligation to continuing with the non-use application."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0319" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:modality "must" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:11a56bd149f712fa77bc2188fa341aad8239ea4709668516aa3a0c6222e32c91" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/4%231> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 319 ;
    tmk:spanStart 50 ;
    tmk:supportingText "Once an opponent has filed a complete notice of opposition (comprised of a notice of intention to oppose and an adequate statement of grounds and particulars) the applicant must file a notice of intention to defend if it wishes to continue with the non-use application." ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

tmka:GR-0320 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0143 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate skos:related ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0153 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual connects the statement with opposing extension of protection through the two-part notice of opposition. The statement is not described as a requirement for obtaining extension of protection."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.4e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the ontology should represent this connection through opposition rather than directly."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0320" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:modality "may" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:4bd0c392125a44efe33f5387504c7fe3b910cfdeeda0899638dac525b854e100" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1%231> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 377 ;
    tmk:spanStart 49 ;
    tmk:supportingText "Any person with legal personality can oppose the registration of a trade mark or the extension of protection to an International Registration designating Australia (IRDA) by filing a notice of opposition. A notice of opposition means a notice of intention to oppose and a statement of grounds and particulars (regs 5.2, 17A.29)." ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

tmka:GR-0321 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0040 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:qualifies ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0153 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual describes inadequacy of the statement as a condition permitting dismissal of the opposition. I read this as the statement's adequacy qualifying the opposition's procedural continuation, rather than as an unconditional requirement established by this sentence."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether qualifies appropriately captures a condition permitting dismissal rather than a general procedural requirement."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0321" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:modality "may" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:d90b057bcae910bf66d5698eff6dc64a108d723d8a688c37ea35655e00fbbf66" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part51/6/6/3> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 171 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "Section 99A and regs 5.8, 9.10, 17A.34B and 17A.48K provide for the Registrar to dismiss an opposition if a statement of grounds and particulars is found to be inadequate." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0323 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0117 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:allocatesTo ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0153 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual expressly assigns responsibility for filing the statement to the potential opponent. I use allocatesTo for this allocation of filing responsibility, not for ownership of the document."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.7e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether allocatesTo encompasses allocation of responsibility for filing an instrument."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0323" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:modality "must" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:98618b605123edf366f898d38372b6761e425e795dd51ed1ccba91aff37ad48e" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1/1/2/1> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 172 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "A statement of grounds and particulars must be filed by the potential opponent within one month from the day the notice of intention to oppose is filed (regs 5.7, 17A.34A)." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0324 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0153 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:appliesTo ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0097 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual expressly identifies filing the statement as a purpose for which an extension of time can be sought. The relation applies to the filing period, not to the substantive contents of the statement."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether appliesTo can target the document when the extension concerns its filing period."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0324" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:90b1ff81fb0de7d72734489cac5f7a6bc61aec16b2de076dc3525c8a0e6ac768" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1/1/3/2> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 284 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "The application for an extension of time to file a notice of intention to oppose or a statement of grounds and particulars must be filed with the Trade Marks Office in an approved form and accompanied by the relevant fee (see item 6 in Schedule 9 of the Trade Marks Regulations 1995)." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0325 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0134 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate skos:related ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0153 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual connects inadequacy of the statement to an opposition-dismissal decision that may be reviewed by the ART. The connection is mediated by that decision; the statement itself is not identified as the object of review."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.3e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the ontology should retain this indirect connection or represent it only through the reviewable decision."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0325" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:modality "may" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:d90b057bcae910bf66d5698eff6dc64a108d723d8a688c37ea35655e00fbbf66" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part51/6/6/3> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 364 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "Section 99A and regs 5.8, 9.10, 17A.34B and 17A.48K provide for the Registrar to dismiss an opposition if a statement of grounds and particulars is found to be inadequate. The Registrar will notify both parties of the dismissal. An application for review of the Registrar’s decision to dismiss under these grounds may be made to the Administrative Review Tribunal." ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

tmka:GR-0326 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0004 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate tmk:requiresElement ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0154 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The judicial proposition reproduced in the Manual makes a real tangible danger of confusion necessary to establish deceptive similarity. It requires that danger, not proof of actual confusion."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the combined reference to deception and confusion should be represented separately against each concept."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0326" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:modality "must" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:be7ebe89c273e99bd6bdd4f0a39584903353c1236cad36f992403c53c447dcc8" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part26/2%231> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 821 ;
    tmk:spanStart 634 ;
    tmk:supportingText "To show that a trade mark is deceptively similar to another it is necessary to show that a real tangible danger of deception and confusion occurring. A mere possibility is not sufficient." ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

tmka:GR-0327 a tmk:AuthoredAssertion ;
    tmk:assertionObject tmkc:GC-0070 ;
    tmk:assertionPredicate skos:related ;
    tmk:assertionSubject tmkc:GC-0154 ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual connects deceptive similarity with similar goods and services when explaining the protection afforded by registration. The scope described belongs to registration protection rather than clearly to the deceptive similarity test, so a more specific predicate is uncertain."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.6e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether extendsTo is intended to encompass the protective scope associated with a legal test."@en-AU ;
    tmk:extractionMethod "agent_authoring" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0327" ;
    tmk:isStale false ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:e8a08502ada7bbbc7fa36d72ad6bfa96001b0fb869314d2b2cb23c4dc864f0a0" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part48/12%231> ;
    tmk:spanEnd 2071 ;
    tmk:spanStart 1592 ;
    tmk:supportingText "Noting that a trade mark registration for a particular good or service operates to prevent use of a deceptively similar trade mark for that good/service and any similar goods/services or closely related goods/services, the Registrar is unlikely to exercise its discretion to allow a mark to remain on the Register for an unused good/service based solely on the use of the mark for similar goods/services or closely related goods/services for which the mark is already registered." ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

