    tmk:supportingText "a. the Registrar is to consider whether, because of the combined effect of the following: i. the extent to which the trade mark is inherently adapted to distinguish the designated goods or services; ii. the use, or intended use, of the trade mark by the applicant; iii. any other circumstances; the trade mark does or will distinguish the designated goods or services as being those of the applicant;" ;
