tmkc:GC-0131 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:InstrumentOrRecord,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "Summary, not a definition: Summary: A trade mark application is an application seeking registration of a trade mark under section 27, including a representation of the mark and a specification of the relevant goods and/or services."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "application for registration of a trade mark"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "trade mark application"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "gpt-6.1-sol" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Regulations expressly define the term, and section 27 supplies the application requirements and required contents. The application is best treated as an instrument or record, rather than the act of filing or the trade mark sought to be registered. No existing concept covers the general application: divisional and convention applications are more specific concepts, while examination, acceptance and amendment concern its processing. The regulatory definition is substantive rather than merely a direction to another definition, so it is retained as the definition quote."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9.6e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r5.2/trade-mark-application> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Check whether the definition in regulation 5.2 has a limited contextual scope before adopting it throughout the ontology."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0131" ;
    tmk:labelKey "application for registration of a trade mark",
        "trade mark application" ;
    tmk:notLabel "amendment of an application"@en-AU,
        "convention application"@en-AU,
        "divisional application"@en-AU,
        "examination"@en-AU,
        "trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:notLabelKey "amendment of an application",
        "convention application",
        "divisional application",
        "examination",
        "trade mark" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:prefLabelKey "trade mark application" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r5.2/trade-mark-application> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0131 .

tmkc:GC-0181 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:GroundOfRefusal,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "The ground section 41 creates: a trade mark that is not capable of distinguishing the applicant's goods or services. Held apart from the general idea of a ground for rejection (GC-0006) and from the test it turns on (GC-0058, capable of distinguishing), the way the section 43 ground was (GC-0168, ruling A2). Edges whose sentence is about section 41 point here (ruling B4)."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "ground for rejection under s 41"@en-AU,
        "ground for rejection under section 41"@en-AU,
        "grounds for rejection under section 41"@en-AU,
        "objection under s 41"@en-AU,
        "s 41 ground for rejection"@en-AU ;
    skos:broader tmkc:GC-0006 ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "section 41 ground for rejection"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-code-agent-S027" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-10-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 41 creates one of the closed set of grounds, and the Manual names it 'a section 41 ground for rejection' throughout Parts 22 and 23. Until now the vocabulary held its test (capable of distinguishing) and the general ground, and no concept for the ground itself — sections 39, 40, 42 and 44 each had one (review B4)."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 9e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the pre-2013 wording of section 41 (subsections (5) and (6), still applied to applications filed before 15 April 2013, Part 12.9) is the same ground or wants a concept of its own."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0181" ;
    tmk:labelKey "ground for rejection under s 41",
        "ground for rejection under section 41",
        "objection under s 41",
        "s 41 ground for rejection",
        "section 41 ground for rejection" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41> ;
    tmk:notLabel "capable of distinguishing"@en-AU,
        "section 43 ground for rejection"@en-AU,
